@bobylito  Yes that is right the top section will be navigation but want it to relate the search already completed.
The URL can be generated just from the category name, and possibly one day link through the search term!  

I'm using the instantsearch.js library. It's not the React one.

In order to do this you need to create a custom widget. The widget API can be used this way:

```js
var search = instantsearch(/*parameters*/);

var menuContainer = jQuery('.menu');
search.addWidget({
  render: function(opts) {
    var results = opts.results;
    var menuValues = results.getFacetValues('attribute');
    var html = menuValues.map(facetToHTML);
    menuContainer.html(html);
  }
});

function facetToHTML(facet) {
  return '<a href="#">'+facet.name+'</a>';
}
```

Every time there are new results in your search the method `render` of the widget will be called. It extracts the facet values and transform them into HTML string then add it to the DOM.
